- `guard` statements for `b1`: Missing conditions despite source stating "if a production order is received"; variable `v1` is declared but never linked via a `guard` to constrain the XOR split.
- `guard` statements for `b2`: Missing conditions despite source stating "If there are unavailable materials... Alternatively, if there are available goods..."; variable `v2` is declared but unused.
- `precedence(b2, c2)`: Omits documented behavior "a manufacturing order is placed"; the model shortcuts the available-materials path directly to `c2` instead of executing this alternative action.
- `precedence(n4, c1)` & `precedence(c1, n5)`: Breaks source chronology; the text says "update the sales information and proceed to order dispatch", but the model incorrectly merges this path back into `n5` (material check) and forces it through production steps.
- Sequential precedence `n8` → `n9` → `n10` → `n11`: Lacks correct control-flow logic for concurrency; the source explicitly describes simultaneous actions ("At the same time, the stock is updated and the motorcycles are dispatched", "Simultaneously..."), which require an AND-branch/parallel flows rather than linear sequencing.
- `defines(v1, ..., {})` & `defines(v2, ..., {})`: Empty ranges `{}` do not faithfully reflect the boolean/categorical value spaces required by the conditional decision points in the source text.

Structural Check
- [S1] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S2] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n3` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n4` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n6` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> c2` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.